// The canonical Complex family prototype (D197-C, I090-C1). A Complex value is a frozen,
// runtime-minted value whose real and imaginary components are semantic real numbers
// (Integer, Fraction or Float). An exact Integer zero imaginary part is never retained; a
// Float zero imaginary part, of either sign, is. Only the exact recognizer is installed, by
// the runtime, because it must not dispatch on the candidate. Construction, component
// selectors, arithmetic and ordering are not yet defined.
Complex: Number {}
